  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 60af0432a3c869e48a591344a8dafd71, type: 3}
  m_Name: AppCare 3
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  question: "During a follow-up visit, your father\u2019s oncologist asks how the
    new treatment is going at home. You share that while it\u2019s working, the frequent
    dosing schedule makes daily life challenging.\n\n<b>What impact could this feedback
    have?</b>"
  explanation: "Caregiver feedback helps researchers and healthcare teams assess
    how realistic treatment plans are for patients. This can lead to improved instructions,
    better support, and future treatments that are easier to manage at home. Their
    observations highlight what truly works\u2014and what may need to be adjusted\u2014in
    everyday care routines."
  correctAnswer: It highlights real-life challenges that can help researchers improve
    how approved treatments are used.
  incorrectAnswer1: It may cause the doctor to increase the dose or stop the medication
    entirely.
  incorrectAnswer2: "None\u2014treatment plans can\u2019t change after approval."
  incorrectAnswer3: It allows caregivers to change the dosing schedule of approved
    treatments on their own.
  questionRole: Caregiver
  questionType: MultipleChoice
  questionStage: Approval
